from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib,collections,math
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P=R.parent
def read(n):return json.loads((R/n).read_text())
def save(n,x):(R/n).write_text(json.dumps(x,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False),encoding='utf-8')
def sha(p):return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
s=read('SUMMARY.json');c=read('COUNTS.json');ev=read('OAL-EVENTS.json');seams=read('SEAMS.json');pairs=read('ADJACENT-PAIRS.json');splits=read('ALTERNATE-SPLITS.json');alts=read('ALTERNATES.json');h=next(x for x in s if x['reading']=='H');hc=[x for x in c if x['reading']=='H']
rows=json.loads((P/'complete-atlas-v56/ROWS.json').read_text());v=collections.Counter(w for x in rows if x[0]=='H' for w in x[9] if w)
oal_pairs=[x for x in pairs if x['word']=='oal'];save('OAL-CH-PAIRS.json',oal_pairs)
tailtable=[dict(tail=t,alch=h['tails'].get(t,0),alch_share=h['tails'].get(t,0)/h['alch'],ordinary_ch_word='ch'+t,ordinary_count=v['ch'+t],ordinary_share=v['ch'+t]/h['ordinary_ch']) for t in ['edy','dy','y','ey','ol','eol','eg','em']];save('TAIL-COMPARISON.json',tailtable)
astro=next(x for x in hc if x['section']=='Astronomy/Astrology');joined_h=[z for z in seams if z['reading']=='H'];outside_initial=[z for z in ev if z['reading']=='H' and z['section']!='Astronomy/Astrology' and (z['exact'] or z['proper_initial'])]
findings=dict(H_oal_anywhere=39,H_astro_oal_anywhere=12,H_outside_astro=27,H_oal_exact=3,H_exact_astro=0,H_proper_initial=5,H_proper_initial_astro=3,H_initial_including_exact=8,H_noninitial=31,H_alch_tokens=87,H_both_parts_standalone=80,H_source_loci_with_alternate_split=len({z['locator'] for z in splits if z['joined_reading']=='H'}),H_tail_overlap=h['overlap'],H_matched_overlap=None,matched_limitation=h['missing_strata'],H_standalone_component_frequencies={w:v[w] for w in ['al','dal','okal','qokal','sal','oal','cheol','cheg','chem','chdm']},oal_ch_pairs=oal_pairs,astronomy='Not exclusive, but descriptive enrichment remains:12/39anywhere hits against8.05% of tokens. All H hand4 pages in this atlas are in Astronomy/Astrology; cannot separate hand4 preference from section.',seam='Strong candidate segmentation evidence, especially alternate boundary records, but not a universal seam rule. Seven H exceptions retained, including H oalchdm with unattested chdm. No adjudication of physical spaces.',g='Anchor remains oalcheg, candidate split oal|cheg. oal|chem is a separate graphic/transcription sensitivity, not an established replacement or mandatory line-end form.',mansion='No Pleiades or lunar-mansion prediction promoted. Generic oal-as-astronomy-marker fails exclusivity; a specific word or contextual interpretation remains separately testable. Common oal does not by itself establish chance as explanation for three contiguous oalch hits.')
save('FINDINGS.json',findings)
body='<h1>oal and the al|ch seam</h1><p><b>The seam is worth investigating, but oal is not astronomy-exclusive.</b> H has39 oal-containing tokens:12 in Astronomy/Astrology and27 elsewhere. Exact oal appears three times, all outside that section. A boundary-insensitive oal + ch-word pattern also occurs elsewhere.</p><p>Frozen descriptive rules precede this isolated computation. All18 partial reading codes remain separate. No g/m merge, inferred morphology, sounds, star assignment or plant identity. A concurrent audit folder was encountered; this report has its own code, input freeze and outputs.</p>'
body+='<h2>H counts with boundaries explicit</h2><table><tr><th>Section</th><th>Readable tokens</th><th>Exact oal</th><th>Proper initial oal-</th><th>Noninitial oal</th><th>Any oal</th><th>Initial oalch-</th></tr>'
for z in hc:body+='<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(x)+'</td>' for x in [z['section'],z['tokens'],z['exact'],z['proper_initial'],z['noninitial'],z['anywhere'],z['initial_oalch']])+'</tr>'
body+='</table><p>Proper initial excludes exact oal:5 longer forms, versus8 starts if exact oal is included. Noninitial means start index greater than0 and includes word-final oal; an internal substring is not necessarily a linguistic unit. In this H set there is no overlap between initial and noninitial token classes. The12 astronomy hits represent30.8% of39, against8.05% of all H tokens: broad distribution does not mean proportional or no enrichment. Hand, layout and family controls have not established an astronomy effect. H hand4 has no outside-astronomy comparator in the atlas.</p>'
body+='<h2>Direct counterexamples to exclusive oal</h2><table><tr><th>H form</th><th>Locus</th><th>Section</th></tr>'
for z in outside_initial:body+='<tr><td>'+e(z['word'])+'</td><td>'+e(z['locator'])+'</td><td>'+e(z['section'])+'</td></tr>'
body+='</table><p>All three standalone oal locations also have F oal. f23v oaldary has H/C/F/U agreement; f105v oaldar has H/F/T agreement. These are not merely H-only uncertainty cases. Starred paragraphs on f113r are not the astronomical diagrams, despite the section’s marginal stars.</p>'
for l in ['f17v.P.21','f23v.P.5','f86v5.P.26','f105v.P.29','f113r.P.3']:
 body+='<details><summary>'+e(l)+' · all source alternatives</summary>'+''.join('<p>'+e(z['reading']+': '+z['raw'])+'</p>' for z in alts[l])+'</details>'
body+='<h2>The most informative boundary examples</h2><p>f113r.P.3 is H/T oal.chs, F oal.chsaiin and G oal.chr; f17v.P.21 is F oal.cheor versus H/C oal.sheor. If the proposed seam search treats separated oal + ch-words as equivalent to joined forms, it has non-astronomical examples. We retain their actual boundaries rather than automatically joining them.</p>'
body+='<table><tr><th>Reading</th><th>Locus</th><th>Actual adjacent pair</th></tr>'
for z in oal_pairs:body+='<tr><td>'+e(z['reading'])+'</td><td>'+e(z['locator'])+'</td><td>'+e(z['word']+' | '+z['right'])+'</td></tr>'
body+='</table><h2>How much supports al|ch?</h2><p>The leading H pre-alch counts reproduce: empty22/87 (25.3%), d18 (20.7%), ok9 (10.3%), qok6 (6.9%), s4 (4.6%). The corresponding standalone words al, dal, okal, qokal and sal are attested. Overall80/87 H tokens split into two separately attested strings under the frozen first-alch rule. Attestation is permissive: ordinary script sequences can accidentally yield known components, and no matched pseudo-seam controls were scored.</p><p>There are336 within-row H adjacent pairs with an -al word followed by a ch-word. Nineteen distinct H joined-alch source loci have an exact candidate split somewhere in an alternate reading of that row. This is descriptive boundary evidence, not19 independent expert adjudications or guaranteed position matches. Original contexts and ambiguous row alignment remain available.</p>'
for l in ['f26r.P.7','f39r.P.3','f39r.P.4','f107r.P.36','f113r.P.6']:
 body+='<details><summary>'+e(l)+' · joined / separated source readings</summary>'+''.join('<p>'+e(z['reading']+': '+z['raw'])+'</p>' for z in alts[l])+'</details>'
body+='<h3>Seven exceptions under this retrieval</h3><table><tr><th>H token</th><th>Candidate split</th><th>Standalone frequencies</th></tr>'
for z in joined_h:
 if not z['left_frequency'] or not z['right_frequency']:body+='<tr><td>'+e(z['word'])+'</td><td>'+e(z['left']+' | '+z['right'])+'</td><td>'+e(str(z['left_frequency'])+' / '+str(z['right_frequency']))+'</td></tr>'
body+='</table><p>Zero does not prove impossible segmentation: it means absent as a complete standalone token in this reading and corpus. An exception is not repaired by selecting a new boundary after seeing the result.</p>'
body+='<h2>Shared endings are not identical distributions</h2><p>The reported0.68 similarity lacks its metric definition, token/type weighting, corpus selection and handling of damaged tokens. This audit therefore does not claim an exact replication. Using explicit overlap sum(min(p,q)), where1 means identical distributions and0 disjoint support, H scores0.360 against5,820 ordinary initial-ch tokens. This is descriptive, not a calibrated test statistic. Matching section+hand+format cannot produce a fully supported H score: one Balneological/hand2/L2 candidate has no ordinary-ch comparator; that stratum remains missing.</p><table><tr><th>Tail after alch</th><th>alch tail count / share</th><th>Ordinary ch-word</th><th>Count / share</th></tr>'
for z in tailtable:body+='<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(x)+'</td>' for x in [z['tail'],f"{z['alch']} / {100*z['alch_share']:.1f}%",z['ordinary_ch_word'],f"{z['ordinary_count']} / {100*z['ordinary_share']:.1f}%"])+'</tr>'
body+='</table><p>This shows compatibility of available endings, but not equality of frequencies or a universal joining mechanism. Real syntax or register could produce different tail frequencies even if a seam is genuine. Conversely shared tails can result from ordinary script constraints. No causal conclusion from this overlap alone.</p>'
body+='<h2>Keep the astronomy readings separate</h2><table><tr><th>H form</th><th>Candidate split</th><th>Standalone H frequencies</th></tr>'
for z in joined_h:
 if z['word'].startswith('oal'):body+='<tr><td>'+e(z['word'])+'</td><td>'+e(z['left']+' | '+z['right'])+'</td><td>'+e(str(z['left_frequency'])+' / '+str(z['right_frequency']))+'</td></tr>'
body+='</table><p>H cheol is169 tokens, cheg3, chem1 and chdm0. Thus “ordinary chem” is not a frequency claim that transfers unchanged into H. Anchor H/K/U/V oalcheg remains oal|cheg under this candidate split. The earlier image audit left a graphic/encoding relation to m plausible but unproved, and strict line-end-only behavior was contradicted by interior examples. The paragraph H oalchdm remains F/U allchdm.</p><p><a href="../g-ending-audit-v89/report.html">Ending image audit</a> · <a href="../oalch-hermetic-audit-v90/report.html">Earlier counts and reading alternatives</a></p>'
body+='<h2>What follows for the prediction</h2><p>The astronomy-exclusive oal marker prediction is contradicted by its exact and initial occurrences elsewhere. A boundary-insensitive oal+ch pattern is also not exclusive. This weakens the proposed general marker explanation; it does not prove the three joined oalch tokens happened by chance. A restricted combination may be meaningful even when both components are broad. It also does not prove alch is never a unit: no single segmentation has been established.</p><p>No Pleiades/lunar-mansion identification is advanced from these counts. Such a prediction needs a specified diagram referent, ordered locations or other independently assessable correspondence. It cannot be rescued or rejected solely by choosing whichever substring distribution looks best.</p>'
body+='<h2>All reading codes and coverage</h2><table><tr><th>Code</th><th>Readable tokens</th><th>Exact oal</th><th>Proper initial</th><th>Noninitial</th><th>Any oal</th><th>Initial oalch</th><th>alch overlap</th></tr>'
for z in s:body+='<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(x)+'</td>' for x in [z['reading'],z['tokens'],z['exact'],z['proper_initial'],z['noninitial'],z['anywhere'],z['initial_oalch'],'—' if z['overlap'] is None else f"{z['overlap']:.3f}"])+'</tr>'
body+='</table><p>These18 codes have different coverage and editorial dependencies; they are not18 complete independent transcriptions. F has very sparse astronomical coverage. Absences and cross-reading proportions require coverage qualification.</p><h2>Records</h2>'
for n in ['PROTOCOL.json','FREEZE.json','COUNTS.json','SUMMARY.json','OAL-EVENTS.json','SEAMS.json','ADJACENT-PAIRS.json','ALTERNATE-SPLITS.json','OAL-CH-PAIRS.json','TAIL-COMPARISON.json','ALTERNATES.json','FINDINGS.json','VERIFICATION.json']:
 body+='<p><a href="'+n+'">'+n+'</a></p>'
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>oal boundary audit · Reed v93</title><style>body{font:17px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1120px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;background:#f6f2e8;color:#173c38}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}td,th{border:1px solid #abc;padding:8px;text-align:left}h1,h2,h3{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:2em}details{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #abc}a{color:#126151}</style>'+body+'</html>',encoding='utf-8')
save('SHA256SUMS.json',{p.name:sha(p) for p in R.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name!='SHA256SUMS.json'})
print('Report saved with every reading, split exceptions, matched-pool gaps and source alternatives. HTML appearance unreviewed.')
